---
import Layout from "../layouts/Default.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="System requirements — MyBodyPrism"
  description="Hardware and operating-system requirements for the MyBodyPrism Desktop Viewer, Vault Local, and PrismEducate."
>
  <section class="container narrow">
    <h1>System requirements</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      Three products, all free, all Windows. Vault Local installs with the
      viewer; PrismEducate is its own download.
    </p>

    <h2>Desktop Viewer</h2>
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Operating system</th><td>Windows 10 (64-bit) or Windows 11</td></tr>
        <tr><th>GPU (minimum)</th><td>NVIDIA RTX 2060 or better, with current drivers</td></tr>
        <tr><th>GPU (reference)</th><td>NVIDIA RTX 4080 (development reference platform)</td></tr>
        <tr><th>RAM</th><td>16 GB or more</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Disk</th><td>5 GB free for install plus headroom for your scans</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Display</th><td>1920×1080 or higher; HiDPI supported</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Network</th><td>Required for activation; offline use after activation works</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="muted">
      AMD GPUs may work but aren't tested. Integrated GPUs (Intel HD,
      Iris) are not supported for volume rendering and will fall back to a
      CPU pipeline that is too slow for typical scans. macOS and Linux are
      not supported in V1.
    </p>

    <h2>Vault Local</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Installed with the Desktop Viewer, so its requirements are the viewer's.
      It runs a small server on your own computer and opens its pages in your
      browser, so it also needs a current browser — Edge, Chrome or Firefox.
      Allow for disk space for whatever you keep in it, on top of the viewer's.
    </p>
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Operating system</th><td>Windows 10 (64-bit) or Windows 11</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Browser</th><td>A current version of Edge, Chrome or Firefox</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Disk</th><td>Space for your own records, beyond the viewer's install</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Network</th><td>Not required — Vault Local makes no network calls</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>PrismEducate</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      A separate download, and lighter than the viewer: it shows published
      imaging rather than rendering your own scans, so it asks less of your
      graphics card.
    </p>
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Operating system</th><td>Windows 10 (64-bit) or Windows 11</td></tr>
        <tr><th>GPU</th><td>Any current graphics card with up-to-date drivers</td></tr>
        <tr><th>RAM</th><td>8 GB or more</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Display</th><td>1920×1080 or higher; HiDPI supported</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Network</th><td>Required for activation; offline use after activation works</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
      Questions? <a href="mailto:support@mybodyprism.com">support@mybodyprism.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .narrow { max-width: 760px; padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem; }
    th, td {
      padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-border);
      text-align: left;
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    th { width: 35%; background: var(--c-accent); }
    .muted { color: var(--c-muted); font-size: 0.92rem; }
    .lede { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem; }
  </style>
</Layout>
